(*
# ModelDefinition
Decodes one archive of index 7 `MODELS` into the geometry the asset dumpers
consume. A port of `net.runelite.cache.definitions.loaders.ModelLoader`, whose
`decodeType3` and `decodeType2` bodies this file follows statement for statement.

The format is **positional, not opcode-driven**. A 24- or 21-byte header at the
tail of the buffer declares the counts and the byte length of a dozen data
sections; every section offset is then derived by adding those lengths up in a
fixed order, and five (type2) or seven (type3) independent cursors read the
sections in parallel - the same buffer, seven positions. There
is nothing to resynchronise on: get one length wrong and the decode still
"succeeds", producing a plausible-looking model built from the wrong bytes. The
guards against that are in `Load` (the section table must account for exactly
the whole buffer) and in `dev/tests/280_model.simba` (every decoded index must
address a vertex that exists, across all 60484 models).

## Which formats are ported
Only type2 and type3. Across the 60484 models in the live cache the census is
27039 type2, 33445 type3, and zero of anything else; cache 2625 agrees (26990 /
34616 / 0). `decodeType1` and `decodeOldFormat` are therefore **not** ported and
`Load` raises when it meets one, the same choice `TCacheStore` made for the
extended sector format. The format is picked from the last two bytes:

| last two bytes | format |
|---|---|
| `FF FD` | type3 |
| `FF FE` | type2 |
| `FF FF` | type1 - raises |
| anything else | old format - raises |

## Not ported
`computeNormals`, `computeTextureUVCoordinates` and `computeAnimationTables`
run in Java's `load` but nothing in the dump path calls them: the object and NPC
dumps need `Height` and `Colors`, and both read the raw geometry. Porting a
2000-line renderer that no consumer exercises would be dead code.

## Signed narrowing is load-bearing
Java stores face colours and texture ids in `short[]` and priorities,
transparencies and render types in `byte[]`, and the narrowing casts really do
produce negative values: 20392 of the 60484 models in the live cache carry at
least one face colour above 32767, 3518377 faces in all. Two of those signs are
not cosmetic:

- type2 moves the raw face colour into `FaceTextures` and then tests it against
  -1 to decide whether the model has textures at all. Keeping the value
  unsigned turns a raw 65535 ("no texture") into a real texture id.
- `Colors` deduplicates on the face colour, and `ObjExporter` deduplicates on
  the same signed value. Both work as long as the two agree.

So every field Java narrows is narrowed here too. `TIntegerArray` is the carrier
- Lape has no 16- or 8-bit array type and every consumer widens anyway.

## Empty means absent
Java nulls `faceTextures`, `faceRenderTypes` and `textureCoords` at the end of
`decodeType2` when nothing used them, and `Colors` branches on
`faceTextures != null`. Here that is `Length(...) = 0`. The two readings differ
only for a model with `FaceCount = 0` (20 of them in the live cache), where an
allocated array is also empty - and nothing iterates a zero-length model, so the
difference is unobservable.
*)
{$DEFINE WL_CACHE_DEF_MODEL_INCLUDED}
{$IFNDEF WL_CACHE_BYTESTREAM_INCLUDED}{$INCLUDE_ONCE ../bytestream.simba}{$ENDIF}
{$IFNDEF WL_CACHE_JAGEXCOLOR_INCLUDED}{$INCLUDE_ONCE ../jagexcolor.simba}{$ENDIF}
{$IFNDEF WL_CACHE_DEF_TERRAIN_INCLUDED}{$INCLUDE_ONCE terrain.simba}{$ENDIF}

type
(*
## TModelDefinition
```pascal
TModelDefinition = record
  Id, Format: Integer;
  VertexCount, FaceCount, NumTextureFaces: Integer;
  VertexX, VertexY, VertexZ: TIntegerArray;
  FaceIndices1, FaceIndices2, FaceIndices3: TIntegerArray;
  FaceColors, FaceTextures: TIntegerArray;
  FaceRenderPriorities, FaceTransparencies, FaceRenderTypes: TIntegerArray;
  TextureRenderTypes: TIntegerArray;
  TexIndices1, TexIndices2, TexIndices3: TIntegerArray;
  Priority: Integer;
  TextureCoords, PackedVertexGroups, PackedTransparencyVertexGroups: TIntegerArray;
  FaceZOffsets: TIntegerArray;
  AnimayaGroups, AnimayaScales: array of TIntegerArray;
end;
```
Every field `ModelDefinition.java` has that either decoder writes. The `transient`
ones (`vertexNormals`, `faceNormals`, `faceTextureU/VCoordinates`, `vertexGroups`,
`origV*`, `maxPriority`) belong to the renderers that are not ported, and
`texturePrimaryColors` is declared in Java but never written by any loader.

`Format` is 2 or 3 and has no Java counterpart - it is the branch `load` took,
kept because the two formats disagree on which fields exist and a caller that
cares should not have to re-sniff the buffer.

`Priority` is the model-wide fallback, set only when `FaceRenderPriorities` is
absent. Java stores it in a `byte`, so the 128..254 range comes back negative.
*)
  TModelDefinition = record
    Id: Integer;
    Format: Integer;

    VertexCount: Integer;
    FaceCount: Integer;
    NumTextureFaces: Integer;

    VertexX: TIntegerArray;
    VertexY: TIntegerArray;
    VertexZ: TIntegerArray;

    FaceIndices1: TIntegerArray;
    FaceIndices2: TIntegerArray;
    FaceIndices3: TIntegerArray;

    FaceColors: TIntegerArray;
    FaceTextures: TIntegerArray;

    FaceRenderPriorities: TIntegerArray;
    FaceTransparencies: TIntegerArray;
    FaceRenderTypes: TIntegerArray;

    TextureRenderTypes: TIntegerArray;
    TexIndices1: TIntegerArray;
    TexIndices2: TIntegerArray;
    TexIndices3: TIntegerArray;

    Priority: Integer;
    TextureCoords: TIntegerArray;
    PackedVertexGroups: TIntegerArray;
    PackedTransparencyVertexGroups: TIntegerArray;
    FaceZOffsets: TIntegerArray;

    AnimayaGroups: array of TIntegerArray;
    AnimayaScales: array of TIntegerArray;
  end;

// Java's (short) and (byte) narrowing casts. See the unit docstring - the signs
// these produce are read by later branches, they are not decoration.
function ModelToShort(v: Integer): Integer;
begin
  Result := v and $FFFF;
  if Result > $7FFF then Result -= $10000;
end;

function ModelToByte(v: Integer): Integer;
begin
  Result := v and $FF;
  if Result > $7F then Result -= $100;
end;

// Allocate zeroed. SetLength alone keeps whatever the array held before, and
// `Result` in a Lape function can alias a caller variable that is being reused
// in a loop - which is exactly how these records are consumed.
procedure ModelAlloc(var arr: TIntegerArray; count: Integer);
begin
  arr := [];
  SetLength(arr, count);
end;

// Linear scan. Deliberately local: whether Lape's array helpers are available on
// a plain TIntegerArray in this build is unverified, and utils/cache/ units must
// not depend on anything unproven.
function ModelIndexOf(var arr: TIntegerArray; value: Integer): Integer;
begin
  for Result := 0 to High(arr) do
    if arr[Result] = value then Exit;
  Result := -1;
end;

procedure ModelAppend(var arr: TIntegerArray; value: Integer);
begin
  SetLength(arr, Length(arr) + 1);
  arr[High(arr)] := value;
end;

(*
## TModelDefinition.Reset
```pascal
procedure TModelDefinition.Reset(id: Integer);
```
Clears every field. `Load` calls this first because a Lape record's arrays are
shared by reference with whatever variable receives the result, so a record
reused across a loop would otherwise start each decode holding the previous
model's arrays - and `SetLength` preserves the overlapping prefix rather than
zeroing it.
*)
procedure TModelDefinition.Reset(id: Integer);
begin
  Self.Id := id;
  Self.Format := 0;
  Self.VertexCount := 0;
  Self.FaceCount := 0;
  Self.NumTextureFaces := 0;
  Self.Priority := 0;

  Self.VertexX := [];
  Self.VertexY := [];
  Self.VertexZ := [];
  Self.FaceIndices1 := [];
  Self.FaceIndices2 := [];
  Self.FaceIndices3 := [];
  Self.FaceColors := [];
  Self.FaceTextures := [];
  Self.FaceRenderPriorities := [];
  Self.FaceTransparencies := [];
  Self.FaceRenderTypes := [];
  Self.TextureRenderTypes := [];
  Self.TexIndices1 := [];
  Self.TexIndices2 := [];
  Self.TexIndices3 := [];
  Self.TextureCoords := [];
  Self.PackedVertexGroups := [];
  Self.PackedTransparencyVertexGroups := [];
  Self.FaceZOffsets := [];
  Self.AnimayaGroups := [];
  Self.AnimayaScales := [];
end;

(*
## TModelDefinition.DecodeType3
```pascal
procedure TModelDefinition.DecodeType3(data: TByteArray);
```
`ModelLoader.decodeType3`. The 24-byte header sits at `Length(data) - 26`, ahead
of the two-byte `FF FD` marker; the sections it describes run from offset 0 to
that header.

Section order, in the order the offsets are accumulated - this *is* the file
layout, and getting one entry's size or its position in the chain wrong shifts
every section after it:

| section | size | present when |
|---|---|---|
| texture render types | textureCount | textureCount > 0 |
| vertex flags | vertexCount | always |
| face render types | faceCount | hasRenderTypes = 1 |
| face index compression types | faceCount | always |
| face render priorities | faceCount | priority = 255 |
| packed transparency vertex groups | faceCount | hasTexVertexGroups = 1 |
| vertex groups + animaya | vertexGroupLen | always |
| face transparencies | faceCount | hasTransparencies = 1 |
| face index deltas | faceIndexLen | always |
| face textures | faceCount * 2 | hasTextures = 1 |
| texture coords | texCoordLen | always |
| face colours | faceCount * 2 | always |
| vertex X / Y / Z deltas | xLen / yLen / zLen | always |
| texture triples, render type 0 | simpleTex * 6 | always |
| render type 1..3 blocks | complexTex * (6+6+2+1+2), plus type-2 extras | always |
| footer | 1 (+7) (+1) (+faceCount) | always |

The footer is a marker byte (non-zero pulls in a 10-byte vertex offset block),
then a flag byte and, if set, one signed byte of Z offset per face.
*)
procedure TModelDefinition.DecodeType3(data: TByteArray);
var
  s1, s2, s3, s4, s5, s6, s7: TByteStream;
  vertexCount, faceCount, textureCount: Integer;
  hasRenderTypes, priority, hasTransparencies, hasTexVertexGroups: Integer;
  hasTextures, hasVertexGroups, hasAnimaya: Integer;
  xLen, yLen, zLen, faceIndexLen, texCoordLen, vertexGroupLen: Integer;
  simpleTex, complexTex, alphaTex: Integer;
  cursor: Integer;
  offRenderTypes, offFaceIdxTypes, offPriorities, offTexVGroups, offVGroups: Integer;
  offTransparencies, offFaceIdxData, offTextures, offTexCoords, offColors: Integer;
  offVX, offVY, offVZ: Integer;
  offTex0, offTex1, offTex2, offTex3, offTex4, offTex5: Integer;
  i, j, n, flags, dx, dy, dz, px, py, pz: Integer;
  kind, a, b, c, last, swap: Integer;
begin
  s1 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s2 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s3 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s4 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s5 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s6 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s7 := TByteStream.Create(data);

  s1.SetPosition(s1.Length() - 26);
  vertexCount        := s1.ReadUShort();
  faceCount          := s1.ReadUShort();
  textureCount       := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasRenderTypes     := s1.ReadUByte();
  priority           := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasTransparencies  := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasTexVertexGroups := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasTextures        := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasVertexGroups    := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasAnimaya         := s1.ReadUByte();
  xLen               := s1.ReadUShort();
  yLen               := s1.ReadUShort();
  zLen               := s1.ReadUShort();
  faceIndexLen       := s1.ReadUShort();
  texCoordLen        := s1.ReadUShort();
  vertexGroupLen     := s1.ReadUShort();

  simpleTex := 0;
  complexTex := 0;
  alphaTex := 0;
  if textureCount > 0 then
  begin
    ModelAlloc(Self.TextureRenderTypes, textureCount);
    s1.SetPosition(0);
    for i := 0 to textureCount - 1 do
    begin
      // Signed: the counters below compare against 0..3, and Java reads a byte.
      n := s1.ReadByte();
      Self.TextureRenderTypes[i] := n;
      if n = 0 then Inc(simpleTex);
      if (n >= 1) and (n <= 3) then Inc(complexTex);
      if n = 2 then Inc(alphaTex);
    end;
  end;

  cursor := textureCount + vertexCount;
  offRenderTypes := cursor;
  if hasRenderTypes = 1 then cursor += faceCount;
  offFaceIdxTypes := cursor;
  cursor += faceCount;
  offPriorities := cursor;
  if priority = 255 then cursor += faceCount;
  offTexVGroups := cursor;
  if hasTexVertexGroups = 1 then cursor += faceCount;
  offVGroups := cursor;
  cursor += vertexGroupLen;
  offTransparencies := cursor;
  if hasTransparencies = 1 then cursor += faceCount;
  offFaceIdxData := cursor;
  cursor += faceIndexLen;
  offTextures := cursor;
  if hasTextures = 1 then cursor += faceCount * 2;
  offTexCoords := cursor;
  cursor += texCoordLen;
  offColors := cursor;
  cursor += faceCount * 2;
  offVX := cursor;
  cursor += xLen;
  offVY := cursor;
  cursor += yLen;
  offVZ := cursor;
  cursor += zLen;
  offTex0 := cursor;
  cursor += simpleTex * 6;
  offTex1 := cursor;
  cursor += complexTex * 6;
  offTex2 := cursor;
  cursor += complexTex * 6;
  offTex3 := cursor;
  cursor += complexTex * 2;
  offTex4 := cursor;
  cursor += complexTex;
  offTex5 := cursor;
  cursor := cursor + complexTex * 2 + alphaTex * 2;

  Self.VertexCount := vertexCount;
  Self.FaceCount := faceCount;
  Self.NumTextureFaces := textureCount;
  ModelAlloc(Self.VertexX, vertexCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.VertexY, vertexCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.VertexZ, vertexCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceIndices1, faceCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceIndices2, faceCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceIndices3, faceCount);
  if hasVertexGroups = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.PackedVertexGroups, vertexCount);
  if hasRenderTypes = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.FaceRenderTypes, faceCount);
  if priority = 255 then
    ModelAlloc(Self.FaceRenderPriorities, faceCount)
  else
    Self.Priority := ModelToByte(priority);
  if hasTransparencies = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.FaceTransparencies, faceCount);
  if hasTexVertexGroups = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.PackedTransparencyVertexGroups, faceCount);
  if hasTextures = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.FaceTextures, faceCount);
  if (hasTextures = 1) and (textureCount > 0) then ModelAlloc(Self.TextureCoords, faceCount);
  if hasAnimaya = 1 then
  begin
    Self.AnimayaGroups := [];
    Self.AnimayaScales := [];
    SetLength(Self.AnimayaGroups, vertexCount);
    SetLength(Self.AnimayaScales, vertexCount);
  end;
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceColors, faceCount);
  if textureCount > 0 then
  begin
    ModelAlloc(Self.TexIndices1, textureCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.TexIndices2, textureCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.TexIndices3, textureCount);
  end;

  // Vertices: one flag byte per vertex picks which of the three delta streams
  // advance, and each axis is a running total.
  s1.SetPosition(textureCount);
  s2.SetPosition(offVX);
  s3.SetPosition(offVY);
  s4.SetPosition(offVZ);
  s5.SetPosition(offVGroups);
  px := 0;
  py := 0;
  pz := 0;
  for i := 0 to vertexCount - 1 do
  begin
    flags := s1.ReadUByte();
    dx := 0;
    if (flags and 1) <> 0 then dx := s2.ReadShortSmart();
    dy := 0;
    if (flags and 2) <> 0 then dy := s3.ReadShortSmart();
    dz := 0;
    if (flags and 4) <> 0 then dz := s4.ReadShortSmart();

    px += dx;
    py += dy;
    pz += dz;
    Self.VertexX[i] := px;
    Self.VertexY[i] := py;
    Self.VertexZ[i] := pz;
    if hasVertexGroups = 1 then
      Self.PackedVertexGroups[i] := s5.ReadUByte();
  end;

  // Animaya continues in the same stream as the vertex groups.
  if hasAnimaya = 1 then
    for i := 0 to vertexCount - 1 do
    begin
      n := s5.ReadUByte();
      ModelAlloc(Self.AnimayaGroups[i], n);
      ModelAlloc(Self.AnimayaScales[i], n);
      for j := 0 to n - 1 do
      begin
        Self.AnimayaGroups[i][j] := s5.ReadUByte();
        Self.AnimayaScales[i][j] := s5.ReadUByte();
      end;
    end;

  s1.SetPosition(offColors);
  s2.SetPosition(offRenderTypes);
  s3.SetPosition(offPriorities);
  s4.SetPosition(offTransparencies);
  s5.SetPosition(offTexVGroups);
  s6.SetPosition(offTextures);
  s7.SetPosition(offTexCoords);

  for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
  begin
    Self.FaceColors[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
    if hasRenderTypes = 1 then Self.FaceRenderTypes[i] := s2.ReadByte();
    if priority = 255 then Self.FaceRenderPriorities[i] := s3.ReadByte();
    if hasTransparencies = 1 then Self.FaceTransparencies[i] := s4.ReadByte();
    if hasTexVertexGroups = 1 then Self.PackedTransparencyVertexGroups[i] := s5.ReadUByte();
    // Stored one higher than the id, so 0 means "no texture" and lands on -1.
    if hasTextures = 1 then Self.FaceTextures[i] := ModelToShort(s6.ReadUShort() - 1);
    // TextureCoords is only allocated when FaceTextures is, so the guard below
    // can dereference it - the same short-circuit the Java relies on.
    if (Length(Self.TextureCoords) > 0) and (Self.FaceTextures[i] <> -1) then
      Self.TextureCoords[i] := ModelToByte(s7.ReadUByte() - 1);
  end;

  // Faces: a per-face compression byte says how many of the three indices are
  // re-read and how the previous triple is rotated into the new one.
  s1.SetPosition(offFaceIdxData);
  s2.SetPosition(offFaceIdxTypes);
  a := 0;
  b := 0;
  c := 0;
  last := 0;
  for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
  begin
    kind := s2.ReadUByte();
    if kind = 1 then
    begin
      a := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      b := s1.ReadShortSmart() + a;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + b;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := b;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;

    if kind = 2 then
    begin
      b := c;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := b;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;

    if kind = 3 then
    begin
      a := c;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := b;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;

    if kind = 4 then
    begin
      // The swap is written back to FaceIndices2, not b: the Java stores the
      // pre-swap value there while b keeps the post-swap one for the next face.
      swap := a;
      a := b;
      b := swap;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := swap;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;
  end;

  // Only render type 0 stores a vertex triple. Types 1..3 have their own blocks,
  // which the offsets above reserve space for and which nothing reads - the Java
  // does not decode them either.
  s1.SetPosition(offTex0);
  s2.SetPosition(offTex1);
  s3.SetPosition(offTex2);
  s4.SetPosition(offTex3);
  s5.SetPosition(offTex4);
  s6.SetPosition(offTex5);

  for i := 0 to textureCount - 1 do
    if (Self.TextureRenderTypes[i] and 255) = 0 then
    begin
      Self.TexIndices1[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
      Self.TexIndices2[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
      Self.TexIndices3[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
    end;

  s1.SetPosition(cursor);
  n := s1.ReadUByte();
  if n <> 0 then
  begin
    s1.ReadUShort();
    s1.ReadUShort();
    s1.ReadUShort();
    s1.ReadInt();
  end;

  if s1.ReadUByte() = 1 then
  begin
    ModelAlloc(Self.FaceZOffsets, faceCount);
    for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
      Self.FaceZOffsets[i] := s1.ReadByte();
  end;

  // The footer must end exactly where the header begins. Nothing else in this
  // decoder can fail, so this is the only place a mis-sized section shows up.
  if s1.Position <> s1.Length() - 26 then
    raise 'ModelDefinition: type3 model ' + ToStr(Self.Id) + ' ends at ' +
          ToStr(s1.Position) + ', expected ' + ToStr(s1.Length() - 26);
end;

(*
## TModelDefinition.DecodeType2
```pascal
procedure TModelDefinition.DecodeType2(data: TByteArray);
```
`ModelLoader.decodeType2`. A 21-byte header at `Length(data) - 23`, ahead of the
`FF FE` marker, and five cursors instead of seven.

Two structural differences from type3 rather than just a shorter header:

- **Textures ride on the face colours.** There is no separate texture stream. A
  face flag byte with bit 1 set moves that face's colour into `FaceTextures` and
  replaces the colour with 127. `hasRenderTypes` therefore gates all three of
  `FaceRenderTypes`, `TextureCoords` and `FaceTextures`.
- **Three arrays are dropped again at the end.** If no face turned out to use a
  render type, a texture or a distinct texture coordinate, Java nulls the whole
  array. `Colors` reads `FaceTextures` through exactly that test, so the drop is
  not cosmetic: a model where every textured face was folded away must come back
  with no textures at all.

`TextureCoords` is dropped by a different rule from the other two - a coordinate
is cleared when its texture triple already equals the face's own vertex triple,
and only if *every* coordinate clears does the array go.
*)
procedure TModelDefinition.DecodeType2(data: TByteArray);
var
  s1, s2, s3, s4, s5: TByteStream;
  vertexCount, faceCount, textureCount: Integer;
  isTextured, priority, hasTransparencies, hasTexVertexGroups: Integer;
  hasVertexGroups, hasAnimaya: Integer;
  xLen, yLen, zLen, faceIndexLen, vertexGroupLen: Integer;
  cursor: Integer;
  offVertexFlags, offFaceIdxTypes, offPriorities, offTexVGroups, offTexFlags: Integer;
  offVGroups, offTransparencies, offFaceIdxData, offColors, offTexTriples: Integer;
  offVX, offVY, offVZ: Integer;
  i, j, n, flags, dx, dy, dz, px, py, pz: Integer;
  kind, a, b, c, last, swap, coord: Integer;
  usesRenderTypes, usesTextures, usesTexCoords: Boolean;
begin
  s1 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s2 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s3 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s4 := TByteStream.Create(data);
  s5 := TByteStream.Create(data);

  s1.SetPosition(s1.Length() - 23);
  vertexCount        := s1.ReadUShort();
  faceCount          := s1.ReadUShort();
  textureCount       := s1.ReadUByte();
  isTextured         := s1.ReadUByte();
  priority           := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasTransparencies  := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasTexVertexGroups := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasVertexGroups    := s1.ReadUByte();
  hasAnimaya         := s1.ReadUByte();
  xLen               := s1.ReadUShort();
  yLen               := s1.ReadUShort();
  zLen               := s1.ReadUShort();
  faceIndexLen       := s1.ReadUShort();
  vertexGroupLen     := s1.ReadUShort();

  offVertexFlags := 0;
  cursor := offVertexFlags + vertexCount;
  offFaceIdxTypes := cursor;
  cursor += faceCount;
  offPriorities := cursor;
  if priority = 255 then cursor += faceCount;
  offTexVGroups := cursor;
  if hasTexVertexGroups = 1 then cursor += faceCount;
  offTexFlags := cursor;
  if isTextured = 1 then cursor += faceCount;
  offVGroups := cursor;
  cursor += vertexGroupLen;
  offTransparencies := cursor;
  if hasTransparencies = 1 then cursor += faceCount;
  offFaceIdxData := cursor;
  cursor += faceIndexLen;
  offColors := cursor;
  cursor += faceCount * 2;
  offTexTriples := cursor;
  cursor += textureCount * 6;
  offVX := cursor;
  cursor += xLen;
  offVY := cursor;
  cursor += yLen;
  offVZ := cursor;
  cursor += zLen;

  Self.VertexCount := vertexCount;
  Self.FaceCount := faceCount;
  Self.NumTextureFaces := textureCount;
  ModelAlloc(Self.VertexX, vertexCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.VertexY, vertexCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.VertexZ, vertexCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceIndices1, faceCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceIndices2, faceCount);
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceIndices3, faceCount);
  if textureCount > 0 then
  begin
    ModelAlloc(Self.TextureRenderTypes, textureCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.TexIndices1, textureCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.TexIndices2, textureCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.TexIndices3, textureCount);
  end;
  if hasVertexGroups = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.PackedVertexGroups, vertexCount);
  if isTextured = 1 then
  begin
    ModelAlloc(Self.FaceRenderTypes, faceCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.TextureCoords, faceCount);
    ModelAlloc(Self.FaceTextures, faceCount);
  end;
  if priority = 255 then
    ModelAlloc(Self.FaceRenderPriorities, faceCount)
  else
    Self.Priority := ModelToByte(priority);
  if hasTransparencies = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.FaceTransparencies, faceCount);
  if hasTexVertexGroups = 1 then ModelAlloc(Self.PackedTransparencyVertexGroups, faceCount);
  if hasAnimaya = 1 then
  begin
    Self.AnimayaGroups := [];
    Self.AnimayaScales := [];
    SetLength(Self.AnimayaGroups, vertexCount);
    SetLength(Self.AnimayaScales, vertexCount);
  end;
  ModelAlloc(Self.FaceColors, faceCount);

  s1.SetPosition(offVertexFlags);
  s2.SetPosition(offVX);
  s3.SetPosition(offVY);
  s4.SetPosition(offVZ);
  s5.SetPosition(offVGroups);
  px := 0;
  py := 0;
  pz := 0;
  for i := 0 to vertexCount - 1 do
  begin
    flags := s1.ReadUByte();
    dx := 0;
    if (flags and 1) <> 0 then dx := s2.ReadShortSmart();
    dy := 0;
    if (flags and 2) <> 0 then dy := s3.ReadShortSmart();
    dz := 0;
    if (flags and 4) <> 0 then dz := s4.ReadShortSmart();

    px += dx;
    py += dy;
    pz += dz;
    Self.VertexX[i] := px;
    Self.VertexY[i] := py;
    Self.VertexZ[i] := pz;
    if hasVertexGroups = 1 then
      Self.PackedVertexGroups[i] := s5.ReadUByte();
  end;

  if hasAnimaya = 1 then
    for i := 0 to vertexCount - 1 do
    begin
      n := s5.ReadUByte();
      ModelAlloc(Self.AnimayaGroups[i], n);
      ModelAlloc(Self.AnimayaScales[i], n);
      for j := 0 to n - 1 do
      begin
        Self.AnimayaGroups[i][j] := s5.ReadUByte();
        Self.AnimayaScales[i][j] := s5.ReadUByte();
      end;
    end;

  s1.SetPosition(offColors);
  s2.SetPosition(offTexFlags);
  s3.SetPosition(offPriorities);
  s4.SetPosition(offTransparencies);
  s5.SetPosition(offTexVGroups);

  usesRenderTypes := False;
  usesTextures := False;
  for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
  begin
    Self.FaceColors[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
    if isTextured = 1 then
    begin
      flags := s2.ReadUByte();
      if (flags and 1) = 1 then
      begin
        Self.FaceRenderTypes[i] := 1;
        usesRenderTypes := True;
      end
      else
        Self.FaceRenderTypes[i] := 0;

      if (flags and 2) = 2 then
      begin
        Self.TextureCoords[i] := ModelToByte(flags shr 2);
        Self.FaceTextures[i] := Self.FaceColors[i];
        Self.FaceColors[i] := 127;
        // The colour was a signed short, so a raw 65535 arrives here as -1 and
        // means "no texture after all".
        if Self.FaceTextures[i] <> -1 then
          usesTextures := True;
      end
      else
      begin
        Self.TextureCoords[i] := -1;
        Self.FaceTextures[i] := -1;
      end;
    end;

    if priority = 255 then Self.FaceRenderPriorities[i] := s3.ReadByte();
    if hasTransparencies = 1 then Self.FaceTransparencies[i] := s4.ReadByte();
    if hasTexVertexGroups = 1 then Self.PackedTransparencyVertexGroups[i] := s5.ReadUByte();
  end;

  s1.SetPosition(offFaceIdxData);
  s2.SetPosition(offFaceIdxTypes);
  a := 0;
  b := 0;
  c := 0;
  last := 0;
  for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
  begin
    kind := s2.ReadUByte();
    if kind = 1 then
    begin
      a := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      b := s1.ReadShortSmart() + a;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + b;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := b;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;

    if kind = 2 then
    begin
      b := c;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := b;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;

    if kind = 3 then
    begin
      a := c;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := b;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;

    if kind = 4 then
    begin
      swap := a;
      a := b;
      b := swap;
      c := s1.ReadShortSmart() + last;
      last := c;
      Self.FaceIndices1[i] := a;
      Self.FaceIndices2[i] := swap;
      Self.FaceIndices3[i] := c;
    end;
  end;

  // type2 has no per-texture render type in the file: every triple is type 0.
  s1.SetPosition(offTexTriples);
  for i := 0 to textureCount - 1 do
  begin
    Self.TextureRenderTypes[i] := 0;
    Self.TexIndices1[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
    Self.TexIndices2[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
    Self.TexIndices3[i] := ModelToShort(s1.ReadUShort());
  end;

  s1.SetPosition(cursor);
  if s1.ReadUByte() = 1 then
  begin
    ModelAlloc(Self.FaceZOffsets, faceCount);
    for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
      Self.FaceZOffsets[i] := s1.ReadByte();
  end;

  if s1.Position <> s1.Length() - 23 then
    raise 'ModelDefinition: type2 model ' + ToStr(Self.Id) + ' ends at ' +
          ToStr(s1.Position) + ', expected ' + ToStr(s1.Length() - 23);

  // Post step: drop the three arrays nothing turned out to use.
  if Length(Self.TextureCoords) > 0 then
  begin
    usesTexCoords := False;
    for i := 0 to faceCount - 1 do
    begin
      coord := Self.TextureCoords[i] and 255;
      if coord <> 255 then
      begin
        if (Self.FaceIndices1[i] = (Self.TexIndices1[coord] and $FFFF)) and
           (Self.FaceIndices2[i] = (Self.TexIndices2[coord] and $FFFF)) and
           (Self.FaceIndices3[i] = (Self.TexIndices3[coord] and $FFFF)) then
          Self.TextureCoords[i] := -1
        else
          usesTexCoords := True;
      end;
    end;
    if not usesTexCoords then Self.TextureCoords := [];
  end;

  if not usesTextures then Self.FaceTextures := [];
  if not usesRenderTypes then Self.FaceRenderTypes := [];
end;

(*
## TModelDefinition.Load
```pascal
function TModelDefinition.Load(id: Integer; data: TByteArray): TModelDefinition; static;
```
Decodes one MODELS archive. Every archive in index 7 holds a single file, so
`data` is `TCacheStore.Read(Ord(EIndexType.MODELS), id, [])` - there is no
reference-table lookup and no archive split.

Raises on a type1 or old-format model rather than decoding it, and on a model
whose section sizes do not add up to its buffer.
*)
function TModelDefinition.Load(id: Integer; data: TByteArray): TModelDefinition; static;
var
  n: Integer;
begin
  Result.Reset(id);

  n := Length(data);
  if n < 2 then
    raise 'ModelDefinition: model ' + ToStr(id) + ' is ' + ToStr(n) + ' byte(s), too short to carry a format marker';

  if (data[n - 2] = $FF) and (data[n - 1] = $FD) then
  begin
    Result.Format := 3;
    Result.DecodeType3(data);
  end
  else if (data[n - 2] = $FF) and (data[n - 1] = $FE) then
  begin
    Result.Format := 2;
    Result.DecodeType2(data);
  end
  else if (data[n - 2] = $FF) and (data[n - 1] = $FF) then
    raise 'ModelDefinition: model ' + ToStr(id) + ' is type 1, which is not ported'
  else
    raise 'ModelDefinition: model ' + ToStr(id) + ' is in the old format, which is not ported';
end;

(*
## TModelDefinition.Height
```pascal
function TModelDefinition.Height(): Integer;
```
`ObjExporter.getSimbaHeight`: the vertical extent of the model in game units,
measured over the negated Y axis because model space grows downwards.

**The two seeds are not neutral, and this is not a rounding detail.** `hi` starts
at 0 and `lo` at Java's `0xffffffff`, which as a signed int is **-1, not MaxInt**.
Neither can be moved the wrong way, so any model that does not already straddle
both bounds measures wider than it is: 45605 of the 60484 models in the live
cache are one unit taller than their real extent because no vertex reaches
`-y = -1`, and 429 more are stretched by the `hi` seed. An empty model measures
1, not 0.

Reproducing that inflation is the whole point - it is what the committed
`wasp-assets` heights contain, so "fixing" either seed breaks parity with every
object and NPC size the pipeline has ever published.
*)
function TModelDefinition.Height(): Integer;
var
  i, hi, lo, current: Integer;
begin
  hi := 0;
  lo := -1;
  for i := 0 to High(Self.VertexY) do
  begin
    current := Self.VertexY[i] * -1;
    if current > hi then hi := current;
    if current < lo then lo := current;
  end;
  Result := hi - lo;
end;

// TextureManager.findTexture: by definition id, not by position. The ids have a
// gap (54 is missing from the live cache), so indexing the array by id would
// return the wrong texture for every id above the gap - and 84 models really do
// change colour if you get this wrong.
function ModelFindTextureRGB(var textures: array of TTextureDefinition; id: Integer): Integer;
var
  i: Integer;
begin
  if (id >= 0) and (id <= High(textures)) and (textures[id].Id = id) then
    Exit(textures[id].AverageRGB);

  for i := 0 to High(textures) do
    if textures[i].Id = id then
      Exit(textures[i].AverageRGB);

  raise 'ModelDefinition: no texture with id ' + ToStr(id);
end;

(*
## TModelDefinition.Colors
```pascal
function TModelDefinition.Colors(textures: array of TTextureDefinition): TIntegerArray;
```
`ObjExporter.getSimbaColors`: the model's palette as packed BGR, in the order the
faces first introduce each colour. This is the `colors` array the object and NPC
dumps carry.

Per face, a textured face contributes its texture's average colour and an
untextured one its own HSL, both at `JAGEX_BRIGHTNESS_MAX`, converted to BGR.
There are three separate deduplications and they are not equivalent:

1. a texture id already seen is skipped,
2. a face colour already seen is skipped,
3. a BGR value already in the result is not appended again.

The first two are *continues* - they skip the face entirely - while the third
only suppresses the append. Two different HSL values that gamma-correct to the
same BGR are therefore recorded in `knownHSL` twice but appear once, which is
what makes the result a set while the palette order stays first-seen order.

`textures` is a parameter rather than a global: the dumpers hold one texture
list and a model is meaningless without knowing which. Pass the full index 9
archive 0 list with each definition's real `Id` - the lookup is by id.

Note `AverageRGB` is a 16-bit field, so its red channel is always 0 before the
brightness pass. That is what `TextureDefinition.averageRGB` holds in Java too.
*)
function TModelDefinition.Colors(textures: array of TTextureDefinition): TIntegerArray;
var
  i, textureId, rgb, bgr: Integer;
  knownTextures, knownHSL: TIntegerArray;
begin
  Result := [];
  knownTextures := [];
  knownHSL := [];
  for i := 0 to Self.FaceCount - 1 do
  begin
    textureId := -1;
    if Length(Self.FaceTextures) > 0 then
      textureId := Self.FaceTextures[i];

    if textureId <> -1 then
    begin
      if ModelIndexOf(knownTextures, textureId) <> -1 then Continue;
      rgb := JagexAdjustForBrightness(ModelFindTextureRGB(textures, textureId), JAGEX_BRIGHTNESS_MAX);
      ModelAppend(knownTextures, textureId);
    end
    else
    begin
      if ModelIndexOf(knownHSL, Self.FaceColors[i]) <> -1 then Continue;
      rgb := JagexHSLtoRGB(Self.FaceColors[i], JAGEX_BRIGHTNESS_MAX);
      ModelAppend(knownHSL, Self.FaceColors[i]);
    end;

    bgr := JagexRGBtoBGR(rgb);
    if ModelIndexOf(Result, bgr) = -1 then
      ModelAppend(Result, bgr);
  end;
end;
